  "subject": "Who Sets AI’s Content Rules?",
  "date": "Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:30:40 -0400",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n Media is becoming a test case for AI. Media Trends Executive Preview \r\n Media Is Testing AI’s New Rules \n\n Media Trends Executive Preview Media is Testing AI's New Rules\n\n \r\n \r\n Some of AI’s biggest unresolved questions are playing out in the media industry first: What can models learn from? Who should get paid? And which deals could become the template for everyone else? \n\n &nbsp;\n\n \r\n On Sept. 19, Media Trends Executive members will receive the first installment of a two-part deep dive examining how publishers, AI companies and Hollywood are beginning to answer these questions.&nbsp; \n\n \r\n&nbsp;\n\n What to watch: \n\n \r\n Copyright law meets borderless technology. Models can train on content legally in one country and operate in another, putting decades of copyright and fair-use precedent to the test. \r\nNew payment models are emerging . Publishers and AI companies are experimenting with retrieval-based agreements that could compensate content owners based on actual usage. \r\nHollywood could set an important precedent . Studio deals are beginning to define how companies can adopt AI while protecting valuable creative IP.&nbsp; \r\n For anyone tracking where AI regulation, business models and intellectual property go next, media offers an early look at the rules taking shape. \n\n &nbsp;\n\n \r\n Become a Media Trends Executive member to get the full deep dive on Sept. 19, plus part two of our AI series in October. \n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Join Media Trends Executive \r\n \r\n &#8202; \r\n Media Trends Executive maps where strategy is shifting and what it signals for media, tech, and entertainment leaders. Join now and unlock industry deep dives, platform updates, and forward-looking analysis from Sara Fischer and Kerry Flynn.&nbsp;\r\n\n &#8202; \r\n \r\n \r\n PO Box 101060 \n Arlington VA 22201 \n\n \r\n Contact Us \n Update Preferences \n\r\n Unsubscribe \n\n LinkedIn \n\n \r\n Facebook \n X \n\r\n Instagram \n\n PO Box 101060\nArlington VA 22201\n\n \r\n \r\n Contact Us \n Update Preferences \n\r\n Unsubscribe \n\n \r\n LinkedIn \n\n Facebook \n\r\n Twitter \n\n Instagram",
